nfection without localizing signs or microbiologic evidence", "Autoimmune Hemolytic Anemia: Could explain anemia and constitutional symptoms but lacks supporting lab markers (e.g., reticulocytosis, Coombs positivity)", "Metabolic Syndrome: Diabetes history is present but weight loss + blasts suggest neoplastic processes rather than primary metabolic derangement"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (weight loss, fever, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia with blasts (hematologic alarm sign)", "Acute visual changes (headache + blurry vision)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.13128171135268712, "posterior": 0.2065916343123999, "danger": 0.95, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["35% circulating myeloid blasts is a pathognomonic feature for myeloid neoplasm. This finding provides direct morphologic evidence for the diagnosis."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.27042797953980474, "posterior": 0.0803498681060418, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["35% circulating myeloid blasts is a pathognomonic feature for myeloid neoplasm. This finding provides direct morphologic evidence for the diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4330611868972258, "posterior": 0.32744640279534365, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Acute constitutional symptoms and no prior CML history disfavor chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3) and favor myeloid blast-related conditions (B1.1, B1.…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urgency", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.081, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal calcium and lack of bone marrow findings (not explicitly described) do not support plasma cell disorders. This weakly argues against B4."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.001, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["35% blasts is a definitive malignant threshold. This strongly excludes reactive leukocytosis."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.09908053686995255, "posterior": 0.18757949479705674, "danger": 0.95, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Acute constitutional symptoms and no prior CML history disfavor chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3) and favor myeloid blast-related conditions (B1.1, B1.…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "CML in Blast Crisis", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.019, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No prior CML history weakly argues against CML in blast crisis (B1.2), though blast crisis can occur without documented chronic phase."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (MDS-EB)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal MCV and marrow morphology do not exclude MDS-EB (B1.3), but they reduce its likelihood. MDS-EB typically presents with dysplastic features."]}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (B-Cell or T-Cell Variant)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.25239944757048444, "posterior": 0.07579639160008954, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["35% myeloid blasts strongly disfavor ALL (B2.1) and lymphoblastic lymphoma (B2.2), which typically present with lymphoid blasts."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (T-Cell or B-Cell Variant)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.005, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of lymphoma-specific features weakens lymphoblastic lymphoma (B2.2) as a diagnosis, though it remains a minor possibility."]}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2", "B3", "B1.1", "B2.1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset over days with constitutional symptoms argue against de novo AML in favor of a chronic process like CML in blast crisis?", "summary": "Subacute symptoms are more typical of phase transformations (e.g., CML in blast crisis, B1.2) than de novo AML, but the blast count remains pathognomonic for myeloid processes."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented prior chronic myeloid leukemia history rule out chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis as the diagnosis?", "summary": "No prior CML history weakly argues against CML in blast crisis (B1.2), though blast crisis can occur without documented chronic phase."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of abnormal mean corpuscular volume or bone marrow morphology rule out myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts (MDS-EB)?", "summary": "Normal MCV and marrow morphology do not exclude MDS-EB (B1.3), but they reduce its likelihood. MDS-EB typically presents with dysplastic features."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 35% myeloid blasts in the lab results disfavor acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) in favor of myeloid processes?", "summary": "35% myeloid blasts strongly disfavor ALL (B2.1) and lymphoblastic lymphoma (B2.2), which typically present with lymphoid blasts."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of lymphoma-specific findings (e.g., lymphadenopathy, mediastinal mass) rule out lymphoblastic lymphoma as the diagnosis?", "summary": "Lack of lymphoma-specific features weakens lymphoblastic lymphoma (B2.2) as a diagnosis, though it remains a minor possibility."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the acute presentation with weight loss and fever disfavor chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm (CML) in favor of myeloid blast-related conditions?", "summary": "Acute constitutional symptoms and no prior CML history disfavor chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3) and favor myeloid blast-related conditions (B1.1, B1.2)."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.433], ["B2", 0.27], ["B2.1", 0.252]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers present", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading branch (B3) has posterior 0.433 < 0.75, and multiple dangerous alternatives (B1, B2) remain unresolved with posterior >=0.10. Further testing (e.g., bone marrow biopsy, cytogenetics) is needed to distinguish myeloid vs. lymphoid processes and determine phase of disease."}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.8, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.4330611868972258, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Myeloproliferative disorder', 'Multiple myeloma'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": true, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B3", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0